---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { ELSEWHERE } from '../consts';

// One contact route rather than a second copy of the footer's link list.
const linkedin = ELSEWHERE.find((link) => link.label === 'LinkedIn');
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Ryan Nel — a software engineer in Gothenburg who learns by building things."
>
  <h1 class="page-title">About</h1>

  <div class="prose page-prose">
    <p>I’m Ryan. I learn by building.</p>
    <p>
      Reading about something only gets me so far. I understand it properly once I’ve tried to make
      it or use it, got it a bit wrong, and had to work out why. So I usually have a few projects on
      the go.
      Some are software. Some are closer to art: maps, pictures, small ways of telling a story.
    </p>
    <p>
      I’ve started sharing some of my latest work <a href="/projects/">here</a>. Each project comes
      with a write-up of how it was made: what I tried, what didn’t work, and how I got around it.
      If you want to try one out, or make something similar, the code and prompts are usually on
      GitHub and linked in each write-up.
    </p>
    <p>
      At work I’m a Senior Staff Software Engineer at Volvo Cars, and that’s where I put what I’ve learnt to use. A lot of the job is understanding a problem
      properly before solving it: how part of the business works, why a team does things a certain
      way, what people actually need from a system. I spend time with the people who build, run and
      depend on our systems, and work with the people leading our product, business and engineering
      on where those systems go next. I still get into the code when that’s the quickest way to move
      a problem along.
    </p>
    <p>
      Nothing here is about my employer’s work. Where something I learnt at work shows up, it’s in
      general terms.
    </p>
    <p>
      If any of it is useful, or wrong, I’d like to hear about it.{' '}
      {linkedin ? <a href={linkedin.href} rel="me">LinkedIn</a> : 'Get in touch'} is the easiest way
      to reach me.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
